  "answer": "Based on JDPower's own 2014 SUV model listings by brand, **Toyota** released the most SUV models in 2014 with **9 models**.\n\nHere's the count from JDPower.com for each brand:\n\n| Brand | SUV Models (Count) |\n|-------|-------------------|\n| **Toyota** | **9** — 4Runner, FJ Cruiser, Highlander, Highlander Hybrid, Land Cruiser, RAV4, RAV4 EV, Sequoia, Venza |\n| **Nissan** | **8** — Armada, JUKE, Murano, Murano CrossCabriolet, Pathfinder, Rogue, Rogue Select, Xterra |\n| **Ford** | **6** — Edge, Escape, Expedition, Expedition EL, Explorer, Flex |\n| **Jeep** | **6** — Cherokee, Compass, Grand Cherokee, Patriot, Wrangler, Wrangler Unlimited |\n| **Chevrolet** | **5** — Captiva Sport Fleet, Equinox, Suburban, Tahoe, Traverse |\n| **Honda** | **4** — CR-V, Crosstour, Pilot, Ridgeline |\n| **GMC** | **4** — Acadia, Terrain, Yukon, Yukon XL |\n| **Lincoln** | **4** — MKX, Navigator, Navigator L, MKT |\n| **Dodge** | **3** — Durango, Journey, Grand Caravan* |\n| **Cadillac** | **3** — Escalade, Escalade ESV, SRX |\n| **Volkswagen** | **2** — Tiguan, Touareg |\n\n*Grand Caravan is technically a minivan but appears on Dodge's JDPower SUV page.\n\nToyota leads with 9 distinct SUV models listed for the 2014 model year on JDPower's website.",
